From 428dcab736fc65d455f9fbc922c7b0a94c25a215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:07:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(core): pin W^X prot sweep and wait4 pid admission

### What
Sweeps every `prot` combination 0..8 for `mmap` (9) and `mprotect` (10): admission holds iff the bits do not request WRITE and EXEC together, including higher prot bits. Also pins `wait4` pid admission: pid 0 is rejected while `-1` and positive pids are admitted.

### Why it matters
W^X is an isolation invariant of the balanced contract, and `wait4` pid 0 would target a process group the single-task contract does not model. Neither arm had a direct test, so relaxing either passes the existing suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| narrow the W^X mask to `PROT_EXEC` only | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| drop the `wait4` pid check | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-core --lib mmap_mprotect_reject`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
index 1389e2fd..65dbf923 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
@@ -1004,4 +1004,25 @@ mod tests {
         assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 1, 0, 0));
         assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(302, 0, 100, 0));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn mmap_mprotect_reject_wx_and_wait4_rejects_pid_zero() {
+        for prot in 0u64..8 {
+            let wx = prot & 2 != 0 && prot & 4 != 0;
+            assert_eq!(
+                balanced_arguments_allowed(9, 0, 0x1000, prot),
+                !wx,
+                "mmap prot {prot}"
+            );
+            assert_eq!(
+                balanced_arguments_allowed(10, 0, 0x1000, prot),
+                !wx,
+                "mprotect prot {prot}"
+            );
+        }
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(9, 0, 0x1000, 6 | 0x100));
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(SYS_WAIT4, 0, 0, 0));
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(SYS_WAIT4, u64::MAX, 0, 0));
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(SYS_WAIT4, 1, 0, 0));
+    }
 }
